issues.correction:
Plan for one developer plus the AI assistant, with 2 explicit buffer days (10-19, 10-23) and an 'assistant unavailable' contingency (runbooks a human can execute; native CI workflows that need no AI). The one-developer cut list:
- no relay unless a rights-clean source is confirmed by 10-12;
- no LL-HLS steering;
- no admin keyboard;
- no Linux tier;
- no multiblock block port: use a client-anchored display (see the join-lockout issue);
- admin control by command and presets only.
State plainly in the verdict that two people are needed for the full scope.

Put the relay on a separate VPS or CDN, never the game host. Add an ops checklist for the game server:
- max-players raised;
- spawn chunk preloading;
- no scheduled automatic restarts, backups or world saves that pause the server between 14:00 and 01:00 on 10-25;
- a TPS and player-count dashboard;
- a 30+ player join-storm test at G5.

On Windows, install natives to %LOCALAPPDATA%\AkashicWeb\<buildId> (never roaming or OneDrive). Put the profile at %LOCALAPPDATA%\AkashicWeb\profiles\<hash(instanceDir)>, with the ASCII-safe fallback for that path. Add P1 cells:
- an instance under a OneDrive-redirected Documents;
- Controlled Folder Access on;
- a username with an accent AND a space;
- a non-admin Windows account.

Add P1 cells:
- Defender default plus one third-party AV (Avast or Kaspersky);
- one Intel iGPU, one AMD and one NVIDIA;
- an 8 GB RAM machine, where the client defaults to Off or 480p when total RAM is 8 GB or less or -Xmx exceeds 60% of RAM;
- a Linux Wayland session (only if the Linux tier is kept).
Name who owns the macOS test hardware or drop that cell; the placeholder path can be unit-tested by forcing an UNSUPPORTED_OS reason code. Measure the first-init time with Defender and show a progress or 'initializing' placeholder.

At G0, record in writing:
- which server and modpack hosts the telão (GTNH or Forbidden);
- its exact current version;
- the server software (Forge, or a Crucible/Bukkit hybrid, which changes permissions, command handling and plugin interference, e.g. akashic-world-firewall);
- whether players arrive through a Velocity lobby (transfers re-trigger join logic and the browser lifecycle).
Freeze the CURRENT version and never upgrade the server for this event. If Android-launcher players can join, size SN2 and the placeholder for them.

Add P1 cells with Akashic Voice (and AkashicFM, if deployed) co-installed. Mitigate the echo:
- default telão volume lower near spawn;
- a pt-BR 'use fones' notice;
- optionally auto-duck the telão while Akashic Voice reports the local mic as active, via a soft dependency.
Confirm by 10-12 whether AkashicFM is live on the event server; if not, drop SN2 or schedule its deployment explicitly.

